        <h1>LeetCode 3345: Smallest Divisible Digit Product I (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Given two integers n and t, return the smallest integer greater than or equal to n such that the product
                of its digits is divisible by t.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: n = 10, t = 2<br>
                Output: 10<br>
                Explanation: The digit product of 10 is 1*0 = 0, which is divisible by 2, so 10 is already the answer.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int smallestNumber(int n, int t) {
        while (n &lt; 101) {
            int x = n;
            int p = 1;
            while (x &gt; 0) {
                p *= x % 10;
                x /= 10;
            }
            if (p % t == 0)
                return n;
            n++;
        }
        return 0;
    }
};</code></pre>
